# [rc4l] Build context for Dockerfile.game-server. BuildKit reads <dockerfile>.dockerignore in
# preference to the root .dockerignore, which excludes everything (that one serves
# Dockerfile.linux-build, whose image is a toolchain with the source mounted at runtime).
#
# Allowlist rather than denylist, same as Dockerfile.registry.dockerignore. This one has to admit far
# more, because it compiles the whole engine rather than eight files, but the shape is the same: start
# from nothing and name what the build actually reads.
*

!src
!catalogue
!config
!tools
!scripts/game-server-entrypoint.sh
!linux_compile.sh
!LICENSE.txt
!THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt
!README.md

# [rc4l] .git is admitted so the engine's revision_check target can stamp a real revision into
# gitinfo.h. This is not cosmetic here: the registry records iServerRevision from every announce and
# refuses to list servers reporting certain builds, so a server built without a repository is one
# whose identity the registry cannot read.
!.git

# [rc4l] Re-excluded from the directories admitted above. tools/ is admitted for tools/freedoom (the
# shipped IWAD) and tools/gen-wadlists.cmake (read during configure); nothing else in it runs at build
# time, and tools/mcp-bridge in particular is a development harness.
tools/mcp-bridge
tools/data
**/__pycache__

# Build output that would otherwise ride along inside src/ from a local compile.
**/build-linux
**/build-win
**/build-tests
